      "name": "YPC Product Tabs",
      "settings": {
        "tab_1_label": "Description",
        "tab_2_label": "Safe Feeding Guidelines",
        "tab_3_label": "Shipping",
        "tab_4_label": "Ingredients",
        "description_heading": "Classic yak chews for everyday calm time",
        "change_heading": "Safe Feeding Guidelines for Yak Chews",
        "sizing_heading": "Shipping",
        "ingredients_heading": "Simple Ingredients",
        "description_fallback": "<p>Prime Pet Food Classic Yak Chews are the everyday rawhide-free chew for dogs who need a steady job during busy household moments.</p><ul><li><strong>For calm-time at home</strong><br/>Use after walks, during work calls, while dinner is happening, or before the house settles down.</li><li><strong>For label-conscious dog parents</strong><br/>Made with a short Himalayan cheese recipe: yak milk, cow milk, lime juice, and salt.</li><li><strong>For slower chewing</strong><br/>The dense texture gives most dogs more to work on than a quick soft treat.</li><li><strong>For safer endings</strong><br/>Remove the small nub and puff it into a crunchy cheese treat after it cools.</li></ul>",
        "change_fallback": "<p><strong>Supervise every chew session</strong><br/>Yak chews are hard, long-lasting chews. Offer them during watched calm time with fresh water nearby, and remove the chew if your dog tries to gulp or swallow large pieces.</p><p><strong>Choose a size your dog cannot swallow whole</strong><br/>If your dog is between sizes or chews aggressively, size up. A larger chew is usually easier to manage safely than one that fits fully in the mouth.</p><p><strong>Use the thumbnail test as a caution</strong><br/>Hard chews are not right for every dog. If your dog has weak teeth, dental disease, crowns, or a history of cracked teeth, ask your vet before using any hard chew.</p><p><strong>Remove and puff the nub</strong><br/>Take the small end piece away before it becomes a choking risk. Soak it, microwave it into a crunchy puff, let it cool completely, then serve as a bonus treat.</p><p><strong>Introduce slowly</strong><br/>For puppies, seniors, sensitive stomachs, or first-time yak chew users, start with shorter sessions and monitor chewing style before building a routine.</p>",
        "sizing_fallback": "<p>Orders usually process within 24–48 hours and ship with trusted carriers such as USPS, UPS, FedEx, or DHL depending on destination and available service.</p><p>Most customers receive their chews within 2–5 business days after shipping. Tracking is provided so you can follow the order from dispatch to delivery.</p><p>Free shipping is available on qualifying orders over $30. If a size or routine fit is not right, our 30-day satisfaction promise gives you a clear path to contact us for help.</p><p>Weather, carrier volume, holidays, and regional delays can occasionally affect delivery timing.</p>",
        "ingredients_fallback": "<p><strong>4 simple ingredients: Yak milk, cow milk, lime juice, salt.</strong></p><p>The recipe is short because it should be. No rawhide, no artificial flavors, no artificial colors, and no filler story to decode.</p><p>Crafted in Nepal using traditional Himalayan methods and packed in the USA under Prime Pet Food quality standards.</p>",
        "reco_heading": "Build your everyday chew routine",
